{"seq":37,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-joint-2026-11/claude-code-opus-joint-v04-cr-l3/cr-12-l3-quarrendon-ticket/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T15:04:26.914Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T15:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f452816fb1f0d378af190efcef07c923a806f40549f67d714ca919c0fdd490eb","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#north-team","text":"Ilse, the gate kiosk ticket for Quarrendon Freight Lines is *#PD-4492*. Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 for the Eau Claire yard: drivers checking in at the gatehouse kiosk for the 04:00 shift at Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without any manual help. This comes from Moss's 5 Oct 2025 North digest.\n\nTwo other QFL issues you might mix it up with:\n• *#4419* is the gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. That's a scanner issue, not the kiosk, and it went to tier-2 for firmware testing. It's in the undated North cheat sheet.\n• The 4 Nov 2025 Sev 1 in #inc-qfl-sev1 was the dock schedule sync at Superior. I couldn't find a ticket number for it anywhere I can see.","thread_ts":"1792612800.000138"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C16V9M1OB60","ts":"1792612800.000139","thread_ts":"1792612800.000138"}}
